    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nMiniComment\n\n### Description\n\nHey, this opens the door to workflows like aborting visual commenting when the start and end of the visual range reside in different filetypes.\r\n\r\nThe hacky work around would be to return \"%s\" but that's not actually aborting anything and a change that does nothing gets inserted into the undo history.\r\n\r\nI suggest passing an `abort` function into the pre hook, calling it should stop any further code execution:\r\n```lua\r\n  MiniComment.config = {\r\n    hooks = {\r\n      pre = function(abort) end,\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\nlmk what you think.",
    "closed_at": "2022-08-12T15:16:17Z",
