        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Yes I mostly encounter it with filetypes like `svelte`, `vue`, and `html` with embedded `css` or `js`.\r\n\r\nI see. Do you use something like [JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring](https://github.com/JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring)?\r\n\r\n> That means if I wanted to abort I'd have to cause a error right?, It's a good thing to have but I don't think it's how we should abort.\r\n\r\nThat is the idea. The only downside I see to this is that \"true\" errors will be ignored. At the moment I like this more than calling hooks with arguments.",
