            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I see. Do you use something like [JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring](https://github.com/JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring)?\r\n\r\nYes\r\n\r\n> That is the idea. The only downside I see to this is that \"true\" errors will be ignored. At the moment I like this more than calling hooks with arguments.\r\n\r\nThat's my concern as well.\r\nWhy is calling a hook with an argument discouraged?\r\nBtw I was the guy who requested passing session data as an argument into session hooks, Did those cause an issue?",
