            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Yes I like that more, to better bullet proof this lets have a constant say\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> MiniComment.ABORT = \"MiniCommentABORT\"\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> And if that's returned we abort.\r\n\r\nThat seems to only complicate things without obvious gain. It would make sense to add a specially recognized return value only if something special will be done with it. Having false-ish value mean \"stop execution\" seems to be good and intuitive enough.\r\n\r\nI'll work on this in a couple of days.",
